license: AGPL-3.0-only
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
  Classical wave-envelope analogy toy, synthetic only. No claim
  about real atoms, real electromagnetism, or quantum mechanics.
abstract: >-
  A classical wave toy on a 2D disk: a decaying radial envelope times
  a helical spiral phase. Discrete modes ("atoms") are selected by a
  frozen closure gate (integer azimuthal number, integer number of
  spiral pitches across the disk radius), and a stated resolution rule
  measures how envelope decay changes the resolved closure set.
  Standard library only.
